A constant template is finished during compilation.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    title #= "Moth"

    heading #= [$md:
        # [title]
    ]
]

Direct top-level const templates contribute to an active root. The Alpha
compiler uses activity-based entry selection. A direct const root `$in` insert
supplies builder metadata, while an ordinary const fragment renders into the
body. General `$entry` purpose validation remains queued, and the former `$page`
metadata design is superseded by builder slots.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    #[$in title:About]
    #[$in stylesheets:[@styles/site.css]]

    #[$md:
        # Compile-time heading
    ]
]

Only a direct root insert reaches builder routing. Nested and stored inserts
remain ordinary template composition. Scalar builder values concatenate, and
each stylesheet insert needs one tracked CSS resource. The HTML builder
deduplicates stylesheets by resource origin.

Runtime top-level named builder inserts are not supported, and their final
design remains unsettled.

Assigned or returned templates remain ordinary values, not direct page fragments.

Const template loops have an iteration limit so an accidental build-time loop
cannot run forever.
